  "fields": {
    "title": "Keyframe Animation",
    "textContent": {
      "nodeType": "document",
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Description",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Keyframe Animations allow you to create a sequence of style changes. You define different stages (keyframes) of the animation, and ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "3TBGoqMl1snjRBxLIzrc6Z",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "CSS",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": " smoothly moves the element through each stage. This works similar to setting keyframes in after effects, except you write down the different keys for frames instead of clicking them in an ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "1DDBuJHPyDiiT0BOAEo8V6",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "GUI",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ". As they are only done with code, they are also better for the performance of your website then e.g. a mp4 or gif file.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Possibilities",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Keyframe Animations help make web pages more engaging and interactive by adding movement and visual interest without requiring a lot of coding. You can animate nearly every parameter you can set in CSS. The animation can loop, have easings, fixed iterations or a delay. You can even do 3D looking animations with help of parameters like ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "rotate3d().",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Keep in mind that animations can be problematic for people with cognitive concerns, if they contain blinking and flashing elements. Additionally, certain kinds of motion can be a trigger for vestibular disorders, epilepsy, and migraine and Scotopic sensitivity.",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "heading-3",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Example",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "nodeType": "paragraph",
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "Here is a simple example of how you can use keyframes to animate the ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "AbOSsxIGAkVSMh1dhVbK4",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "margin ",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": "of a ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink",
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "4kGIsFGp1lhyqYgaVV5ANk",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "nodeType": "text",
                  "value": "paragraph",
                  "marks": [],
                  "data": {}
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "nodeType": "text",
              "value": ". ",
              "marks": [],
              "data": {}
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "codeField": {
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "code"
                }
              ],
              "value": "css\n/* keyframe name | duration | easing-function | delay |\niteration-count | direction | fill-mode | play-state | name */\np {\n    animation: wiggle 10s ease-in-out infinite;\n}\n\n@keyframes wiggle {\n    0% {\n        margin-left: 4em;\n    }\n    50% {\n        margin-left: 12em;\n    }\n    100% {\n        margin-left: 4em;\n    }\n}",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "nodeType": "document"
    },
